Summary of changes made during the port
---------------------------------------

  * De-domained. agora-lab's engine is coupled to its research-lab vocabulary; the port
    is not. `layout.ts` no longer branches on the roles `supervisor` / `research-staff` /
    `student` / `paper-reviewer` — occupants declare a structural group instead
    (`office` | `workspace` | `annex`). `characterSync.ts` no longer imports
    `AgentRuntimeStatus` from `@agora-lab/core`; its six statuses collapse into the four
    behaviourally distinct activities `gathering` | `busy` | `available` | `away`.
    `Character` lost its required `name` and `role` fields in favour of an optional
    `label`, and `FurnitureInstance.interactive` is a free-form tag rather than the
    `'kanban' | 'meeting'` literal union.

  * Framework-free. Nothing under this directory imports React, and no upstream React
    component was ported.

  * Renames. `LabLayout` -> `OfficeLayout`, `createLabLayout` -> `createOfficeLayout`,
    `syncCharactersToAgents` -> `syncCharactersToOccupants`, `DeskPosition.name` ->
    `DeskPosition.id`, and `spriteData.ts`'s `CHARACTER_PALETTES` ->
    `CHARACTER_SPRITE_PALETTES` (it collided with the unrelated export of the same name
    in `assets.ts`). Files are kebab-cased to match the surrounding codebase.

  * Deletions. `layout.ts`'s dead `getDeskPositions()` / `getMeetingPositions()` helpers
    (hard-coded coordinates unrelated to the computed layout) and its unused `WALL`
    constant are gone.

  * Additions. `sprites.ts` guards a null 2D context instead of asserting non-null;
    `particles.ts` gained `clearParticles()`; `render-policy.ts` exports its two
    signature functions so the dirty-check is directly testable.

  * Preserved deliberately. `characterSignature()` in `render-policy.ts` and the
    `shouldRedraw` / `shouldRedrawCanvas` dirty-check built on it are upstream's
    low-motion performance design and were kept intact.
